<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="hero-stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Features</p>
    <h1>Small phone.<br><em>Real tools.</em></h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      Ei Void is not a chat window pretending to be an IDE. It is a tool-using
      agent with a repository on disk, a real git client and a firm hand on the
      boundary.
    </p>
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/download">Get the preview</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/docs/getting-started">Build it <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">Inside the shell</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Everything the agent can touch.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        The model chooses tools; the tools are typed and guarded. The loop is
        small enough to explain, and the boundary is boring on purpose.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <% features.forEach(function (feature) { %>
        <article class="feature">
          <p class="feature-index"><%= feature.index %></p>
          <h3><%= feature.title %></h3>
          <p><%= feature.body %></p>
        </article>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">The loop</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Watch the tools, not the magic.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        Every step is a tool call you can see. Nothing is pushed until you
        confirm it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <%- include('partials/how') %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">Tiers</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Three temperatures, one router.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        A tier is a promise about effort, not a model name. The router picks
        the exact provider and model, and the usage ledger keeps score.
      </p>
    </div>
    <%- include('partials/tier-grid') %>
    <div class="section-cta">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/pricing">See what each plan includes <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="shell narrow center">
    <p class="kicker">One more thing</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">The cat is not decoration.</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      Gatete is the reminder that a coding agent should feel like a companion,
      not a control panel. The chalk lines are the interface; the void is the
      quiet around it.
    </p>
    <div class="page-actions center-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/#waitlist">Join the preview</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/bot">Meet the Discord bot <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
